      "key": "withdrawal",
      "name": "Primary off",
      "expected": "Every link to CHR 1 loses carrier at once, as on a real power loss. CHR 2 sees its peer port ether2 go down and reverts its MLAG bonds to its own LACP system ID, so the access switch and traffic host 2 renegotiate LACP, with brief loss. They drop their member to CHR 1 on carrier loss, without waiting for the LACP short timeout. With protocol-mode=none no port changes state and no BPDUs appear.",
